<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX5-QA2-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX5-QA2-004" ;
  triage:title "record_task_outcome does not count an emitted prompt in stats.prompted when the durable record_reminder write fails, so the per-tick budget under-counts real prompts (Property 5); no fault-injectable TaskStore double exists to test it" ;
  triage:description "AX.5 QA-2 (quality-mgr ax5-qa-r2, PR #1201 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T14:22Z) at head fbee74ba8a9abf0b3e04b01bc157b8a65f194119. req-qa ATM-QA-006, corroborated by rust-qa-agent QA-003 and rust-service-hardening-agent RSH-102: in record_task_outcome (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs:513-540) the early-return branch taken when record_task_reminder fails stamps last_task_attempt (correct after AX5-QA1-005) but skips the stats.prompted/task_reminders increments, so a Herdr prompt that was actually emitted during a store outage does not count toward HERDR_MAX_PROMPTS_PER_TICK and the tick can over-prompt. Zero test coverage: the suite has no fault-injectable TaskStore double. Fix: increment stats.prompted (and task_reminders) for Emitted regardless of the durable write result, add a failing-write TaskStore test double, and add a test proving the budget still holds when writes fail." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "REQ-QA" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
